==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Drunken Master Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Dancer Cat''' when obtained from [[Kung-Fu Awakens!]] (may drop on the first stage but guaranteed on the second) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
This Cat is a powerful all-around unit, useful for delivering good damage from some range. Basically, the only negatives about Kung Fu Cat are that he is expensive and has a slow recharge time, at least while you are in [[Empire of Cats]]. For [[Into the Future]], [[Cats of the Cosmos]] and [[Legend Stages]], Kung Fu's use becomes more centered as a suicidal attacker, as he does not have enough knockbacks to be anything else.

In early stages, Kung Fu Cat is essentially a more attack-oriented version of [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cat]], meaning he still is good for dealing with hordes of enemies but lacks the health to be useful against bosses with high DPS. Usually, he is used for dealing damage without being knocked back. However, he has to be timed well to get an attack in, or else he will almost definitely die before he can deal damage. A plus for using his first form is that his attack foreswing is much shorter than his True Form's, making him more useful on stages like [[Houses of the Holy]] and [[Heavenly Tower]] [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 30|Floor 30]] for clearing peons if his Immune to [[Wave Attack|Waves]] [[Talents|Talent]] has not been unlocked.

==='''True Form'''===
Dancer Cat's True Form is somewhat lackluster, removing his multi-hit, giving him immunity to Weaken, and increasing his range by 30. His stats are still not worth the cost by the time this form is unlocked, so there is little reason to hurry in doing so. Nevertheless, the loss of multi-hit and the added range can make Dancer Cat useful in certain {{4c}} stages. His immunity to Weaken allows him to get easier hits on [[Calamary]] and sometimes [[Winged Pigge]], but beware his singular knockback and unimpressive health.

His [[Cat Combo]] [[Feel the Dance (Combo)|Feel the Dance]] can be used to great effect in many stages, especially if the Cats involved are raised to their full potential. However, without his Talents, his stats pale in comparison to other conventional midrangers, such as [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], so if you want the best out of him, consider investing into them.

==='''Talents'''===
Before anything else becomes worth considering, Dancer Cat's stats need to be made viable with the Attack Buff and optionally his Defense Buff Talents. The stat buffs make him a much more viable unit to bring into battle, no longer being dwarfed by other midrangers. Immune to Waves turns Dancer Cat into a miniature [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Heroic Musashi]], giving him a very good role as an anti-Waver for {{4c}} Legend Stages due to his disposability and stackability. Freeze Immune is helpful for countering [[Henry]], but is otherwise not as valuable as Wave Immune. His [[Surge Attack|Surge]] ability is rather unique in that it always spawns outside his attack range, allowing him to randomly hit backliners too, but the low activation chance makes it hardly worth the NP.

==='''Orb'''===
Dancer would benefit the most from a Cost Down orb, mainly due to being a generalist that lacks CC abilities.

