==Trivia==
*The outfit worn by Kung Fu Cat looks similar to the iconic yellow jumpsuit that [[wikipedia:Bruce Lee|Bruce Lee]] wears in the movie [[wikipedia:Game of Death|''Game of Death'']].
**In fact, Kung Fu Cat's jumpsuit is colored yellow in [[Nyanko Defence Force]] and [[Go! Go! Pogo Cat]].
*Drunken Master Cat is based on the [[wikipedia:Zui quan|zui quan (醉拳)]] fighting style, which means "drunken fist" in Chinese.
**It may also be a reference to the martial arts comedy film [[wikipedia:Drunken Master|''Drunken Master'']].
*Dancer Cat's appearance and animations are a reference to the late singer [[wikipedia:Michael Jackson|Michael Jackson]].
**His walk animation is an obvious reference to the [[wikipedia:Moonwalk (dance)|Moonwalk]] dance, while his Idle and Knockback animations reference moves performed in his "[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h_D3VFfhvs4 Smooth Criminal]" music video.
*Kung Fu Cat has the highest [[Cat Food]] cost of all purchasable Special Cats.
*Dancer Cat is one of the few Cat Units whose icon is not flipped. This might be due to him normally facing the base and not the enemies, unlike most Cat Units and even his Normal and Evolved Forms.
*Since he faces backwards, Dancer Cat would theoretically be one of the few units who would suffer the intended effect of [[Lord Gravey]]'s [[wikipedia:Kanchō|''kanchō'']] prank.
*Prior to Drunken Master Cat getting multihit in [[Version 6.0 Update|6.0]], it had one attack as strong as that of first form, but later in the animation like the largest attack is now, making for a slight difference between forms.
*In The Battle Cats Unite!, its True Form is still playable, however, it is only obtainable via save file editing.
*Prior to [[Version 15.6 Update|Version 15.6]], Kung Fu Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Kung Fu Cat
Mid-range attack specialist. (Area Attack)
Can fight off multiple enemies at once.</pre>
<pre>Drunken Master Cat
Adopted Drunken Fist style ?
… or just on a bender? (Area Attack)</pre>
<pre>Dancer Cat
A legendary dancer who infuses his strikes
with fiery passion. So shy that he mastered
walking backwards to avoid eye contact. (Area)</pre>

